      "receiptId": "dorset-apple-cake.html-1",
      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt from the Derby Daily Telegraph - Monday 02 November 1925",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003EDorset Apple Cake.\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\nMiss Hetty King, the famous male impersonator, declares that she is deeply fond of cooking, and offers her own recipe for Dorset Apple Cake.\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\nThe ingredients required are: 8oz. self-raising flour. 1 egg. 4oz. margarine. gill milk. 4oz. castor sugar. \u00BE lb. apples.\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\n1. Rub margarine into flour, add sugar and apples cut into cubes. 2. Mix with beaten egg and milk. 3. Butter a shallow cake tin and spread mixture over it. 4. Bake a moderate oven for one hour. Cut squares.\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\nIn Dorset the cake is eaten hot, but it is equally pleasant when it is cold.\u003Cbr\u003E"
    }
  ],
